==Government and politics==
{{Main|Politics of Potocsí}}

Potocsí is a [[unitary state|unitary]] [[presidential system|presidential]] [[republic]]. The [[President of Potocsí|President]] is both [[head of state]] and [[head of government]], elected by [[popular vote]] for a six-year term. The president appoints the [[cabinet]] ({{lang|ca|Consell de Ministres}}) and serves as commander-in-chief of the [[Potocsino Armed Forces|Armed Forces]].

The [[legislature]] is the [[National Congress of Potocsí|National Congress]] ({{lang|ca|Congrés Nacional}}), a [[bicameral]] body consisting of the [[Senate of Potocsí|Senate]] ({{lang|ca|Senat}}, upper house) and the [[Chamber of Deputies of Potocsí|Chamber of Deputies]] ({{lang|ca|Cambra de Diputats}}, lower house). The Senate has 54 members (three per state plus two for indigenous representation), while the Chamber of Deputies has 207 members elected by [[proportional representation]].

The [[judiciary]] is headed by the [[Supreme Tribunal of Justice (Potocsí)|Supreme Tribunal of Justice]] ({{lang|ca|Tribunal Suprem de Justícia}}), whose magistrates are elected by the National Congress for 12-year terms.

